<title>USA: Escalade Inc acquires equipment maker.</title>
<headline>Escalade Inc acquires equipment maker.</headline>
<dateline>EVANSVILLE, Ind. 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Escalade Inc, which makes sporting goods and office machines and equipment, said Tuesday its Martin Yale Industries Inc unit acquired Master Products Manufacturing, a manufacturer of paper punches and catalog rack systems, from James Crean International BV.</p>
<p>Financial terms of the cash transaction were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Master Products had net sales of about $10 million in 1996, Escalade said.</p>
<p>Escalade shares were unchanged a 9-11/16 Tuesday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
